# Repository-wide end-of-line policy.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` every text file lands in the
# working tree with CRLF endings. That is harmless for the SPA sources, but it
# is fatal for the shell scripts in this repository: they are executed by bash
# on WSL and on the droplet (`deploy/deploy.sh`, `scripts/dev-stack.sh`,
# `scripts/test/*`), and a CRLF script dies with
#
#   bash: scripts/test/lib/10-services.sh: line 33: syntax error near
#   unexpected token `$'{\r''
#
# Note that unlike PowerShell (which tolerates CRLF inside scripts), bash does
# not: the `\r` becomes part of the token. Forcing LF in the repository (and in
# every future checkout) removes the whole class of failure — including the
# case where a CRLF copy of a script is rsynced to the droplet.
#
# PowerShell scripts keep CRLF (the native Windows convention; PS 5.1 reads
# both, but CRLF is what every Windows editor expects).

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf

*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.psm1      text eol=crlf
*.psd1      text eol=crlf
